{#
    Tabler HoverGallery — several images in the space of one (`.hover-gallery`,
    Tabler 1.7+): the first one shows, and the image changes as the pointer moves
    across the gallery. No JavaScript; on touch screens it becomes a strip to swipe.

    All-in-one (`images` is an array of {src, alt}):
        <twig:Tabler:HoverGallery indicators class="rounded" images="{{ [
            {src: '/products/backpack-1.jpg', alt: 'Black backpack, front view'},
            {src: '/products/backpack-2.jpg', alt: 'Black backpack, side view'},
        ] }}" />

    Composed (children replace the `content` block):
        <twig:Tabler:HoverGallery indicators class="card-img-top">
            <twig:Tabler:HoverGallery:Item src="/products/watch-1.jpg" alt="Steel watch, front view" />
            <twig:Tabler:HoverGallery:Item src="/products/watch-2.jpg" alt="Steel watch, back view" />
        </twig:Tabler:HoverGallery>

    The gallery is a square; set `--tblr-hover-gallery-aspect-ratio` (e.g. `16 / 9`)
    in a `style` attribute to change the shape. Keyboard users only see the first
    image: keep the information of the others elsewhere on the page.

    Props:
      images      — optional array of {src, alt}, rendered with HoverGallery:Item; mirrored by the `content` block
      indicators  — a bar per image at the bottom edge, lit for the image on display (hover-gallery-indicators)
#}
{% apply trim %}
{% props
    ## list<array{src:string,alt?:string}>|null The images, each rendered with `HoverGallery:Item`.
    images = null,
    ## bool Whether to show a bar per image at the bottom edge, lit for the image on display (`hover-gallery-indicators`).
    indicators = false,
%}

{% set gallery = html_cva(
    base: 'hover-gallery',
    variants: {
        indicators: {true: 'hover-gallery-indicators', false: ''},
    },
) %}

<div class="{{ gallery.apply({indicators: indicators}, attributes.render('class')) }}" {{ attributes.without('class') }}>{## A `HoverGallery:Item` for each entry of `images`; replace it to compose freely. #}
    {%- block content -%}
        {%- for image in images ?? [] -%}
            <twig:Tabler:HoverGallery:Item src="{{ image.src }}" alt="{{ image.alt ?? '' }}" />
        {%- endfor -%}
    {%- endblock -%}
</div>
{% endapply ~%}
